"INFO_SOURCES_2" = "Current radar images: %@. Normally the Showers radar server supplies the images; in case of errors or outdated data, the app loads them directly from the DWD map service by itself.";
"INFO_LINK_DWD" = "German Weather Service (DWD) · Open Data";
"INFO_LINK_DWD_TERMS" = "DWD · Terms of Use";
"INFO_SOURCES_MAPKIT" = "Map and place search: Apple MapKit. The map's attribution notices stay visible.";
"INFO_SOURCES_WARN_AREAS" = "Warning areas (districts and independent cities): Source: Deutscher Wetterdienst, © GeoBasis-DE / BKG 2021 (data modified).";
"INFO_PRIVACY_1" = "No account and no analytics or advertising SDKs. Saved places and custom names stay on your iPhone and your paired Apple Watch; they are not sent to the Showers server.";
"INFO_PRIVACY_2" = "Widgets and Apple Watch use saved places only and fetch their forecasts directly from the DWD. Pairing only transfers the current list of places, no location history. The most recent valid forecast for each place is stored locally for widgets.";
"INFO_PRIVACY_3" = "The app loads radar images from the Showers radar server. The radar service itself keeps no access logs and stores no IP addresses or request details. As with any internet connection, the upstream server technically sees the IP address of your request; radar requests contain no location, no cookies and no identifier. In case of errors or outdated data, the app fetches the radar images directly from the DWD. Images of the additional layers come only from the Showers server. If you show the lightning legend, the app loads the legend image directly from the DWD (for clouds, possibly from EUMETSAT); the provider technically sees your IP address but no location.";
"INFO_PRIVACY_4" = "For a place forecast, the DWD continues to receive a map section around the selected position directly. Maps and search requests are processed by Apple: for place search, the search text and a fixed search area (Germany, not your location) go to Apple, never to the radar service or the DWD; Apple technically sees the IP address. Apple's privacy policy applies.";
"INFO_PRIVACY_5" = "The map on the Apple Watch is loaded through Apple Maps; the coordinate of the place is sent to Apple. The radar images come from the server without any location information.";
"INFO_PRIVACY_6" = "Only if you turn on rain alerts for a place: the Showers server receives your device token, a random installation ID, a grid cell of about 1 km around the place (no coordinates, no place name), and the threshold and lead time; no account. For a region, the server stores a rough area instead: the centre at a coarser resolution than a grid cell (about 2 km), the radius and the trigger share; the name of the region stays on the device. When you turn it off, delete the place or the region, or reset, this data is deleted.";
"INFO_PRIVACY_LOCATION" = "Location access is optional and is only requested when you use it. No background location tracking. Point requests are not stored in an on-disk network cache.";
"INFO_PRIVACY_BETA" = "The app is an early test version. Forecasts may deviate; if data is missing or outdated, no up-to-date statement is guaranteed.";
"INFO_SUPPORT_FOOTER" = "Showers · early test version";
"INFO_LAYER_SOURCES_NOTE" = "The Showers server only provides additional layers (pressure, lightning, clouds, temperature, humidity) if they are enabled there; otherwise they are greyed out. There is no fallback directly from the DWD for them.";
